# Factory defaults that cards from before the factory-applied record get once
# (frontends/retroarch, game-experience-tuning D3 and task 1.4).
#
# A card whose ROMS/system/lume/factory-applied has no line for a file yet (an old card, or a
# core options file the user already had) keeps every value it has: each factory line is
# recorded as applied without touching the card, except the lines listed here, which win
# once over the value RetroArch saved. A factory default added after the record exists needs
# no line here: a factory line missing from the record is applied once on every card that
# has a record for that file.
#
# One "<file-id> <key>" per line. file-id is retroarch.cfg (factory/retroarch/retroarch.cfg)
# or opt:<corename> (factory/retroarch/config/<corename>/<corename>.opt). Every key listed
# must exist in that factory file (tests/unit/test_retroarch_cfg.py).
#
# The left analog stick drives the d-pad (D4): old cards had "0" saved by RetroArch.
retroarch.cfg input_player1_analog_dpad_mode
retroarch.cfg input_player2_analog_dpad_mode
retroarch.cfg input_player3_analog_dpad_mode
retroarch.cfg input_player4_analog_dpad_mode
